title: ch2_truck_spot
---
You pull into the spot outside the hospital at six in the morning. Another truck is already there. #line:ch2_truck_spot_01
Its owner leans out the window. I've parked here for nine years, friend. #line:ch2_truck_spot_02
-> Offer to split the days of the week. #line:ch2_truck_spot_03
    <<choose "share">>
    Mondays to Wednesdays are yours. He even tells you which nurses tip. #line:ch2_truck_spot_04
-> Park there anyway, every day. #line:ch2_truck_spot_05
    <<choose "fight">>
    You get the spot. You also get a parking ticket every week from someone who knows the rules better. #line:ch2_truck_spot_06
-> Find a new corner by the community college. #line:ch2_truck_spot_07
    <<choose "move">>
    Students are broke but loyal. You add a five-dollar plate. #line:ch2_truck_spot_08
===

title: ch2_truck_festival
---
A weekend street festival in Prospect Park offers you a vendor slot. The fee is eight hundred dollars, up front. #line:ch2_truck_festival_01
Last year's vendors say a good truck clears three thousand. A rainy one clears nothing. #line:ch2_truck_festival_02
-> Pay the fee and prep double. #line:ch2_truck_festival_03
    <<choose "go">>
    Sunshine. You sell out by four and still have a line. #line:ch2_truck_festival_04
-> Skip it. Too much risk for one weekend. #line:ch2_truck_festival_05
    <<choose "skip">>
    You spend Saturday with family. Sunday you hear it was a record crowd. #line:ch2_truck_festival_06
===

title: ch2_truck_fdny
---
An FDNY inspector checks the propane tanks on your truck. One valve is past its test date. #line:ch2_truck_fdny_01
-> Close for a day and replace it. #line:ch2_truck_fdny_02
    <<choose "fix">>
    New valve, new certificate, one lost day. You sleep better. #line:ch2_truck_fdny_03
-> Keep working and fix it next month. #line:ch2_truck_fdny_04
    <<choose "tape">>
    He comes back. The fine costs more than the valve ever would. #line:ch2_truck_fdny_05
===

title: ch2_truck_price
---
Chicken prices jumped fifteen percent. Your ten-dollar plate now leaves you two dollars less. #line:ch2_truck_price_01
Unpaid CEO: Eat the cost, cut the portion, or raise the price. Each one teaches you something. #line:ch2_truck_price_02
-> Raise the plate to eleven dollars. #line:ch2_truck_price_03
    <<choose "raise">>
    A few regulars grumble. Almost all of them still order. #line:ch2_truck_price_04
-> Quietly make the portion smaller. #line:ch2_truck_price_05
    <<choose "portion">>
    Nobody says anything. They just come a little less often. #line:ch2_truck_price_06
-> Keep the price and absorb it. #line:ch2_truck_price_07
    <<choose "absorb">>
    Customers stay happy. Your margin gets thinner. #line:ch2_truck_price_08
===

title: ch2_truck_generator
---
The generator coughs, sputters and dies during the lunch rush. Twenty people stare at you. #line:ch2_truck_generator_01
-> Sell cold drinks and chips at a discount. #line:ch2_truck_generator_02
    <<choose "cash_sale">>
    People leave with something and a story. You call a mechanic. #line:ch2_truck_generator_03
-> Buy a new generator today. #line:ch2_truck_generator_04
    <<choose "new">>
    Expensive, but it purrs. No more praying at noon. #line:ch2_truck_generator_05
===

title: ch2_truck_viral
---
A food blogger with a million followers posts your lamb plate. Your phone will not stop buzzing. #line:ch2_truck_viral_01
-> Extend hours and ride the wave. #line:ch2_truck_viral_02
    <<choose "ride">>
    Lines for two weeks. You learn exactly how much one person can grill. #line:ch2_truck_viral_03
-> Keep normal hours and keep quality. #line:ch2_truck_viral_04
    <<choose "steady">>
    Fewer plates than you could sell, but every one is right. #line:ch2_truck_viral_05
===
